<%#
  The same two columns a comparison is read in, empty and waiting to be filled. A box
  on each side you can always type into; a player picked stands as a card, and the
  moment both sides hold one there is a comparison, so the page becomes it. Building
  and reading are the one layout, so moving between them is not a jump.

  The lists below are the pairs our forecast puts closest together, a good list and
  never the pair somebody arrived holding. This is how you reach the one you want.
%>
<section data-controller="comparison-builder"
         data-comparison-builder-url-value="<%= comparison_search_path %>"
         data-comparison-builder-committed-value="false">
  <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-900">Compare any two players, or any two moves</h2>
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-500">
    Start typing a name on each side. A side can hold one player or the several you would
    buy in one move, and once both sides have somebody the comparison opens itself.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:gap-4">
    <% 2.times do |side| %>
      <div data-comparison-builder-target="side" data-side="<%= side %>">
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 empty:hidden" data-comparison-builder-target="chips"></div>

          <div class="relative">
            <label class="sr-only" for="comparison-add-<%= side %>">
              Add a player to <%= side.zero? ? "the first" : "the second" %> side
            </label>
            <input type="text" id="comparison-add-<%= side %>"
                   data-comparison-builder-target="input" data-side="<%= side %>"
                   data-action="input->comparison-builder#search keydown->comparison-builder#keydown"
                   autocomplete="off" placeholder="Add a player"
                   class="w-full rounded-xl border border-dashed border-zinc-300 bg-white px-3 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 placeholder:text-zinc-400 focus:border-zinc-400 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-zinc-900/10">
            <div class="absolute left-0 right-0 top-full z-20 mt-1 max-h-64 overflow-y-auto rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 bg-white shadow-lg"
                 data-comparison-builder-target="results" data-side="<%= side %>" role="listbox" hidden></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-zinc-500" data-comparison-builder-target="hint">Add a player to each side.</p>

  <noscript>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-zinc-500">
      Searching needs JavaScript. The lists below work without it, and so does every
      /compare address once you have one.
    </p>
  </noscript>
</section>
